# AWS 3-Tier Architecture Project

This project demonstrates how to deploy a secure and highly available **3-Tier Architecture on AWS**.

### Screenshot: Architecture

![Screenshot 1 - Architecture](images/Architecture.png)

---

# Architecture Overview

The application is divided into three layers:

## 1. Web Tier

- Two EC2 instances
- Deployed in Public Subnets
- Distributed across two Availability Zones
- Receives user requests through an Application Load Balancer

## 2. Application Tier

- Two EC2 instances
- Deployed in Private Subnets
- Contains the application services
- Not directly accessible from the internet

## 3. Database Tier

- Amazon RDS
- Deployed in Private Database Subnets
- Accessible only from the Application Tier
- Not publicly accessible

---

# Architecture Flow

```text
Users
  |
Internet
  |
Internet Gateway
  |
Application Load Balancer
  |
Web Tier EC2 Instances
  |
Application Tier EC2 Instances
  |
Amazon RDS Database
```

