# Step 8: Launch Web Tier EC2 Instances

Launch two EC2 instances:

```text
Web EC2 1 → Public Subnet 1
Web EC2 2 → Public Subnet 2
```

Install Nginx:

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt install nginx -y
sudo systemctl enable nginx
sudo systemctl start nginx
```

Verify:

```bash
curl http://localhost
```

---

# Step 9: Create Launch Template for Web Tier

Go to:

```text
EC2 Console
→ Launch Templates
→ Create Launch Template
```

Configure:

```text
Launch Template Name: web-tier-launch-template
AMI: Ubuntu
Instance Type: t2.micro
Security Group: Web Tier Security Group
```

## User Data

Use the following script:

```bash
#!/bin/bash

apt update -y
apt install nginx -y

systemctl enable nginx
systemctl start nginx
```

This ensures that every instance launched by the Auto Scaling Group automatically installs and starts Nginx.

---

# Step 10: Create Auto Scaling Group

Go to:

```text
EC2 Console
→ Auto Scaling Groups
→ Create Auto Scaling Group
```

Select:

```text
Launch Template:
web-tier-launch-template
```

Select:

```text
Public Subnet 1
Public Subnet 2
```

Configure capacity:

```text
Minimum Capacity: 1
Desired Capacity: 1
Maximum Capacity: 3
```
